Used, not redistributed
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Model and drafter weights are downloaded by the operator from Hugging Face and are not part of this repository:
RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4 (revision 18d55bfd5a2194887738da73753975c9d3842f46, MIT), quantized from
zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash, with the tokenizer.json of nvidia/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4 (revision
423acf37583782c51c142d145aef733d72943d93, MIT) read in place of its own, and incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2, Inco AI's
DFlash 2 drafter on the DFlash method of z-lab/dflash (Jian Chen, Yesheng Liang, Zhijian Liu) (revision
7d74cdd881ed7e32c31175984a67823127b66cfe, CC BY-NC-ND 4.0: its model card releases the drafter for research and
evaluation). A launch loads both as downloaded; the recipe neither redistributes nor modifies them.
The optional weightless GLP-44 steering of the TP4 profile (off by default; README.md) uses msuiche/weightless
(https://github.com/msuiche/weightless, Matt Suiche; no licence stated): the steering method, its GLM-5.3 patcher
(patches/hotfix-glm53-steering-projective.py at commit 15ed1373f6265c336ef227e7b4280e6ebdd347b3) and the GLP-44
vector msuiche/GLM-5.3-Flash-abliterated-cyber-GLP-44 (Hugging Face, revision
ef85b0169fd25a3c0223eedddee124cf6b1580dc, GLM-5.3-Flash-abliterated-cyber-GLP-44-L1-44-a2.gguf, MIT, gated). The
operator fetches both (the vector with their own Hugging Face token); launch/options/weightless/prepare.py applies
the patcher's replacements on the operator's machine, reading its strings without running it. This repository
contains none of weightless's code or data: the recipe's own guards, the ownership fix and the notice line it adds
are Apache-2.0 (the repository licence), and the lines it replaces are named by sha256 only.
Benchmarks use RigMark (https://github.com/alexellis/rigmark, MIT), llama-benchy
(https://github.com/eugr/llama-benchy, MIT), tool-eval-bench (https://github.com/SeraphimSerapis/tool-eval-bench, MIT;
scenario methodology adapted from stevibe/ToolCall-15) and the lab's own Python reproduction of the decode benchmark
protocol of MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash); none of their code is in this repository.
bench/results/runs/ holds output files of RigMark and llama-benchy runs, and
bench/results/evidence/tool-eval-bench.json a summary of tool-eval-bench results. docs/credits.md lists every project
this recipe builds on or was compared with.

References to paths such as "outputs/2026-09-24-..." inside served source files point to the lab's research
archive, which is not part of this repository.
